      "typical_award_size": "HCD formula allocations to the County: $226,380 (CY 2024) and $238,273 (CY 2025), with an estimated $1,414,875 for the 2024-2028 cycle; the City of Madera receives its own allocation ($296,439 in 2024, $317,530 in 2025; estimated $1,852,744 for 2024-2028). The County's PLHA five-year plan and activity choices were not located (County website blocked).",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not applicable.",
      "affordability_requirement": "PLHA Guidelines Section 301: rental activities must be affordable to extremely low, very low, low or moderate income households (up to 120% AMI), and workforce rental and ownership activities may serve households up to 120% AMI; plans must prioritize households at or below 60% AMI. Rental projects need a 55-year regulatory agreement and PLHA must be a low-interest deferred loan to the sponsor.",
